A||N||4||Lou Christopher||Aluminum Radiators||||1||
Z||000000||Lou Christopher||09-05-2001||11:23 AM||||This is a follow up on my posting earliar about cooling my V 8 Fiero and my search for Aluminum radiators.  I Have looked everywhere that I can find.  Results are as follows:<BR>         Griffin Radiator-$400 for custom<BR>         Howe- offered only stock sixes $300<BR>       Sperior Rad-  $400 for custom size<BR>  Pme dist-18 3/4" X 25 3/4 X 2 1/4 are $195<BR>B Cool and other mfgs only offered stock sizes that would not fit.<P>I did find two mfgs who would make a custom radiators at a resonable price.  The first is Ron Davis Racing products in Ariz. Phone 623-877-5000.  Tim is the contact  Will make Fiero size single or dual pass systems for $280. <BR>   The second is Bryn Mc Cullogh 826-258-6723  he will make a custom size, including custom inlet outlets and location of radiator cap and overflow tube for $270.<BR>   In all cases we are talking about a two core 3" thick radiator, all aluminum, all welded construction.  The consesus of opinion from all mfgs is that 4 core is not the way to go because of reduced air folw.  The 4 core will buy you time before overheating but will probably overheat when a good two core would not.<BR>  I wanted to submit this in case the info would be helpfull to anyone.  I ordered a radiator from Mc Cullogh.  will take two days to make and ship.  hope it does the job.<BR>Thanks again to all who responded to my first call for info.<BR>                 Lou Christopher<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TONY_C||09-05-2001||11:43 AM||||Lou,<BR>thanks for all the info. I would like to hear how the radiator performs when you install it.  I see you are from NY, where about is that?<BR>I'm on Long Island.||||reg||1
